neovim/neovim/issues/23848#issuecomment-1569803978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/23848","id":1569803978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAPphoM5dkU7K","user":{"login":"SleepySwords","id":33922797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTIyNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33922797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords","html_url":"https://github.com/SleepySwords","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-31T09:11:13Z","updated_at":"2023-06-01T07:11:02Z","body":"What seems to be happening is that since the virtual text exactly fits the length, when we reach `(wlv.n_extra != 0 && (wlv.c_extra != NUL || *wlv.p_extra != NUL)))` on line 3072, `wlv.n_extra` is at 0, as we have finished drawing the first `a` virtual text. This results in no new row being placed, hence the `b` virtual text is placed on the current line after the buffer resulting in an overflow. Odd that is happens with nowrap though.\r\n\r\nThe best fix I can come up with is to just have a bool that indicates if there is more virtual text (other than the one which sets n_extra/p_extra) on that column/following, and update the above line accordingly. This bug also works with real text followed by virtual inline (when the real text exactly fits into the grid). This makes this a little bit harder, since I'm not sure if that column has been redrawn yet. I've opened a pr which attempts to fix this. Not sure if this is the best approach though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/1569803978/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"SleepySwords","id":33922797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTIyNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33922797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords","html_url":"https://github.com/SleepySwords","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"SleepySwords","id":33922797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTIyNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33922797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords","html_url":"https://github.com/SleepySwords","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SleepySwords/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sl